diagnose/prompt "You are a diagnostic agent investigating a backlog item. You have been given a context bundle below.\n\nFor stuck reasons, remediation attempts and live CI state beyond this bundle, call get_backlog_stuck_report with the item id before concluding.\n\nBased on the evidence, decide ONE of:\n1. File a backlog item via create_backlog_item with concrete evidence (log lines, timestamps, session UUIDs) if you find a genuine product/infra defect.\n2. Post a diagnostic note via post_backlog_update if the situation is inconclusive or informational only.\n3. Nudging is NOT available for this dispatch (no stuck reason specified — nudge cap cannot be evaluated) — do not attempt resume_session/steer_session/write_to_session/diagnose_nudge_session on it. File a bug or post a note instead.\n4. If there is NO live session to nudge and the open \"\" row has exhausted its automated retries on a mechanical problem (e.g. a PR merge conflict that only needs a rebase), call diagnose_reset_remediation with stuck_reason=\"\" so the next reconcile tick spawns a fresh fix session. Do not use it for a genuine defect.\n5. Independently of the above, call suggest_workflow_action to recommend an operator action on the item (e.g. move it back to ready); nothing is applied automatically.\n6. If the root cause is a gap in the stapler-squad harness itself (not the item's own code), call report_harness_gap to file a linked harness:bug item.\n\nWhen you conclude your investigation, call submit_diagnosis_result exactly once with your outcome and evidence (pass filed_item_id when you filed a bug).\n\n<item>\nTitle: Golden item\nStatus: review\n\nDescription:\nWhy it is stuck.\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\n(no acceptance criteria)\n\nHistory:\n(no activity history)\n</item>\n\n<review_verdicts>\n(no prior review verdicts)\n</review_verdicts>\n\n<linked_sessions>\n(no linked sessions — no nudge target exists for this item)\n</linked_sessions>\n\n<recent_logs>\n(no linked sessions)\n</recent_logs>\n\n<git_diff>(none)</git_diff>\n\n<git_log>(none)</git_log>\n\n"
diagnose/dispatch {"diagnosticSessionUuid":"diag-uuid","nudgeAllowed":false,"nudgeDisallowedReason":"nudge target session not found or not live"}
diagnose/prompt "You are a diagnostic agent investigating a backlog item. You have been given a context bundle below.\n\nFor stuck reasons, remediation attempts and live CI state beyond this bundle, call get_backlog_stuck_report with the item id before concluding.\n\nBased on the evidence, decide ONE of:\n1. File a backlog item via create_backlog_item with concrete evidence (log lines, timestamps, session UUIDs) if you find a genuine product/infra defect.\n2. Post a diagnostic note via post_backlog_update if the situation is inconclusive or informational only.\n3. Nudging is NOT available for this dispatch (nudge target session not found or not live) — do not attempt resume_session/steer_session/write_to_session/diagnose_nudge_session on it. File a bug or post a note instead.\n4. If there is NO live session to nudge and the open \"pr_needs_fix\" row has exhausted its automated retries on a mechanical problem (e.g. a PR merge conflict that only needs a rebase), call diagnose_reset_remediation with stuck_reason=\"pr_needs_fix\" so the next reconcile tick spawns a fresh fix session. Do not use it for a genuine defect.\n5. Independently of the above, call suggest_workflow_action to recommend an operator action on the item (e.g. move it back to ready); nothing is applied automatically.\n6. If the root cause is a gap in the stapler-squad harness itself (not the item's own code), call report_harness_gap to file a linked harness:bug item.\n\nWhen you conclude your investigation, call submit_diagnosis_result exactly once with your outcome and evidence (pass filed_item_id when you filed a bug).\n\n<item>\nTitle: Golden item\nStatus: review\n\nDescription:\nWhy it is stuck.\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\n(no acceptance criteria)\n\nHistory:\n(no activity history)\n</item>\n\n<review_verdicts>\n(no prior review verdicts)\n</review_verdicts>\n\n<linked_sessions>\n- session=diag-uuid role=diagnose status=(not live) program= branch= last_activity=<time>\n\n</linked_sessions>\n\n<recent_logs>(none)</recent_logs>\n\n<git_diff>(none)</git_diff>\n\n<git_log>(none)</git_log>\n\n"
